content.text:
Use a nested write: call `prisma.guild.update` and put the changes to `premium` inside `data`. For a one-to-one relation, `upsert` updates the record if it exists and creates it if not. Adapted to your schema:

```ts
await prisma.guild.update({
  where: { guildId: "123" },
  data: {
    premium: {
      upsert: {
        create: { active: true, subtype_monthly: true },
        update: { active: true, subtype_monthly: true },
      },
    },
  },
  include: { premium: true },
});
```

If the premium row already exists, you can use `premium: { update: { active: false } }` instead.

The docs example is a `post.update` with a nested `author: { upsert: { create, update } }`. Your code is that example with `guild` and `premium` swapped in. I adapted it myself, so I haven't run it against your schema.

Sources: `apps/docs/content/docs/orm/v7/prisma-client/queries/relation-queries.mdx`, "Nested writes → Update or create a related record" (lines 1016–1047) and "Update a specific related record" (lines 987–1014).

